[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged 412 reports as one known issue. Read by tenant, they are three
different problems. Only the first has a fix queued.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Do not count #4471 as "known" for the second and third problems.
</Callout>

## The split

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

<SplitCounts ticket={4471} issues={{ parser: "https://github.com/titangui/s01e03-4471/issues/1", hint: "https://github.com/titangui/s01e03-4471/issues/2", oneDay: "https://github.com/titangui/s01e03-4471/issues/3" }} />

The table above files the 5 one-day reports under `parser`, by tenant. They are not a swap of day and
month, so the second table counts them apart.

## How we told them apart

- Count by **tenant**: its locale and its booking form. Never by `intakeTag`, which is a guess from
  the reporter's browser. 15 of the 33 hint reports were tagged `parser`.
- Count each report id once. The export repeats 15 of them.
- Read the body when a report does not fit. The 5 one-day reports say "one day off", not "month and
  day swapped".

## Lessons

- Merging by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) hid two bugs inside
  a known one.
- "One ticket per issue" means one per cause, not one per subject.

